Grants
  Held: none. Grants are never saved: a restart, level change, revocation or the kill switch ends
      them [observed: Core policy]
  [on] Protected reads: never granted under Aggressive, not even once: credential files
      (.env, .env.* and .envrc files, also ones created later; not .env.example, .env.sample
      or .env.template; SSH, cloud and CLI tokens) and Corbanu's sign-in, vault, config and history
      stay unreadable to agent commands; switch to Permissive in /security to allow them. On Linux
      and Windows a command is stopped when such a file appears while it runs; a process already
      waiting for that file can read it in the moment before the stop [resolved: level]
  [on] Grant once: lets one command write files that run code later, which Aggressive otherwise
      keeps read-only, and only inside the current folder: git hooks and config kept outside a .git
      folder (a hooks folder set with core.hooksPath, such as Husky's .husky, or a git folder with
      another name), and, when the current folder holds your home folder, your shell and git start-
      up files (such as .zshrc, .profile, .gitconfig and .local/bin), login agents and services,
      and .claude settings. Nothing else changes: credential files and Corbanu's sign-in, vault,
      config and history stay unreadable; Corbanu's own files and the project's .git, .codex
      and .agents stay read-only; other folders and the network stay closed. [resolved: level]

